WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:05.303
A neuron has chosen its receptor.

2
00:00:06.263 --> 00:00:07.803
How does its axon know where to go?

3
00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:11.767
The core rule is one receptor and two glomeruli.

4
00:00:12.627 --> 00:00:15.667
That needs each neuron's axon to find the right target.

5
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:21.267
In 1996, Mombaerts and colleagues swapped receptor genes in mice.

6
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.820
The results suggested that receptor identity is instructive in axon targeting, but

7
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:28.820
not the only factor.

8
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.430
So the receptor is one input among several.

9
00:00:33.483 --> 00:00:37.983
If the receptor helps choose the target, how could it change what the growing axon

10
00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:38.983
carries?

11
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.863
One route runs through cAMP.

12
00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:53.303
Imai and colleagues reported receptor-derived cAMP signals shift guidance molecule

13
00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:54.303
expression.

14
00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:02.067
It also shifts where axons project in the bulb, along the front-to-back axis.

15
00:01:03.117 --> 00:01:08.657
Serizawa and colleagues found four adhesion and guidance molecules whose levels vary

16
00:01:08.657 --> 00:01:09.857
with receptor activity.

17
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.550
How such molecules build the map is covered in the lesson on topographic maps.

18
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:17.890
Now recall the lock.

19
00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.510
Its relay ran through the kinase PERK.

20
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:24.163
The lock's own pathway reaches the wiring too.

21
00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:30.047
Shayya and colleagues reported that different receptor sequences produce different

22
00:01:30.047 --> 00:01:32.267
patterns of stress in developing neurons.

23
00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:38.407
A gene called Ddit3 links PERK signalling to guidance and adhesion genes.

24
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.950
So the stress signal that helps hold the choice can also influence where the axon

25
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.950
goes.

26
00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:46.693
These are mouse reports.

27
00:01:47.573 --> 00:01:50.253
They show a link, not the full rules for building the map.

28
00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.627
The choice and the address can share a signal.

29
00:01:54.587 --> 00:01:57.147
Choosing a receptor helps set where the axon goes.
